error[E0201]: overload set `broken` names unknown method `show_itn`
  --> tests/ui/overload_errors.wid:13:19
   |
13 | overload :broken, :show_itn, :LIMIT, :first_of, :twice, :twice, :double
   |                   ^^^^^^^^^ no method with this name next to the set
   = note: an overload set lists methods declared in the same scope as the `overload` line
help: a similar method exists: `show_int`
   | overload :broken, :show_int, :LIMIT, :first_of, :twice, :twice, :double
   = see `wid explain E0201`

error[E0305]: `LIMIT` is a constant, not a method
  --> tests/ui/overload_errors.wid:13:30
   |
 9 | LIMIT = 3
   | ----- `LIMIT` is declared here
...
13 | overload :broken, :show_itn, :LIMIT, :first_of, :twice, :twice, :double
   |                              ^^^^^^ overload sets list methods
help: list only `def`s declared next to the `overload` line
   = see `wid explain E0305`

error[E0316]: `first_of` cannot be part of an overload set because it has `$` type parameters
  --> tests/ui/overload_errors.wid:13:38
   |
10 | def first_of(xs: []$T) -> T = xs[0]
   |     -------- declared here
...
13 | overload :broken, :show_itn, :LIMIT, :first_of, :twice, :twice, :double
   |                                      ^^^^^^^^^ not allowed in an overload set
   = note: a call picks a member by its argument types, which needs concrete parameter types
help: remove `:first_of` from the set and call it by its own name
   = see `wid explain E0316`

error[E0202]: `twice` is listed twice in `broken`
  --> tests/ui/overload_errors.wid:13:57
   |
13 | overload :broken, :show_itn, :LIMIT, :first_of, :twice, :twice, :double
   |                                                         ^^^^^^ listed again here
help: remove the repeated name
   = see `wid explain E0202`

error[E0316]: `twice` and `double` in `broken` both take (Int)
  --> tests/ui/overload_errors.wid:13:65
   |
13 | overload :broken, :show_itn, :LIMIT, :first_of, :twice, :twice, :double
   |                                                                 ^^^^^^^ no call could choose between these
   |                                                 ------ this member takes the same types
help: change one member's parameter types, or remove it from the set
